# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, in the repo and in the working tree.
# Introduced 2026-08-31 after repeated whole-file merge conflicts caused by CRLF/LF
# flip-flopping (the old .editorconfig forced crlf while other tools wrote lf).
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` checks text out as LF.
# Local repos should also set `git config merge.renormalize true` so merges against
# not-yet-normalized branches don't conflict on endings.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one legitimate CRLF exception — cmd.exe has parsing
# edge cases (goto/labels) with LF-only files. PowerShell is fine with LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Known binary types — never touch (auto-detection would skip these anyway; explicit for safety)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
